{{{{{1<noinclude>|Ability data</noinclude>}}}|Dragon's Rage|{{{2|}}}|{{{3|}}}|{{{4|}}}|{{{5|}}}
|champion     = Lee Sin
|skill        = R
|icon         = Dragon's Rage.png
|blurb        = {{sbc|Active:}} {{ci|Lee Sin}} {{tip|root|roots}} the target enemy {{tip|champion}} and roundhouse kicks them, dealing {{as|physical damage}} and {{tip|airborne|knocking them back}}.
|blurb2      = Enemies that collide with the displaced enemy while it is {{tip|airborne}} are briefly {{tip|airborne|knocked up}} and take {{as|'''bonus''' physical damage}} based on the {{as|primary target's '''bonus''' health}}.
|blurb4      = ''This technique was taught to him by Jesse Perring, although Lee Sin does not kick players off the map.''
|description  = {{sbc|Active:}} '''Lee Sin''' {{tip|root|roots}} the target enemy champion over the cast time, then roundhouse kicks them to deal {{as|physical damage}} and {{tip|airborne|knock them back}} {{tt|up to 800 units|see notes}} {{tt|over {{fd|0.8}} seconds|Estimated}}, rendering them {{tip|airborne}} for 1 second.
|leveling     = {{st|Physical Damage|{{ap|175 to 625}} {{as|(+ 200% '''bonus''' AD)}}}}
|description2 = Enemies that collide with the displaced enemy while it is {{tip|airborne}} take the same damage plus {{as|'''bonus''' physical damage}} and are {{tip|airborne|knocked up}} for 1 second.
|leveling2    = {{st|Collision Physical Damage|{{ap|175 to 625}} {{as|(+ 200% '''bonus''' AD)}} {{as|(+ {{ap|12 to 18}}% of primary target's '''bonus''' health)}}}}
|description3 = If ''Dragon's Rage'' kills the primary target, it will still knock them back, causing the target's corpse to be displaced and collide with enemies it passes through.
|cooldown     = {{ap|110 to 60}}
|cast time    = {{fd|0.25}}
|target range = {{tip|cr|icononly = true}} 375
|collision radius= {{tip|cr|icononly = true}} {{tt|160|Checks for collision every 0.25 seconds, estimated}}
|speed        =
|targeting    = Unit
|affects      = Enemies
|damagetype   = Physical
|spellshield  = True
|spelleffects = aoe
|callforhelp  = True
|notes        = 
* The [[spell indicator]] for this ability also displays the direction for the knock back relative to '''Lee Sin's''' position.
* The {{tip|airborne|displacement's}} direction is decided at the moment of impact and not by '''Lee Sin''' and his target's relative locations at the start of the cast (the only way for '''Lee Sin''' to control where his target is displaced is by using {{si|Flash}} before the cast time of ''Dragon's Rage'' ends).
* If the {{tip|airborne}} debuff is removed from the target, its ability to collide with enemies is removed aswell, even if the target has not come to a stop yet.{{bug|2}}
** The airborne debuff and with it collision of the target remains for the normal duration even if its trajectory is {{tip|airborne|displaced}} by another source (i.e - {{ai|Headbutt|Alistar}}).
** The target may still collide with other enemies for the remaining airborne duration after they reach their destination, as the airborne debuff lasts longer than the displacement.
* The knock back distance is intended to be 800, but due to a bug, this is reduced by up-to the sum of '''Lee Sin's''' and his target's {{tip|gameplay radius}}, depending on how far they are away from one another at the end of the cast time.{{bug}}
* ''Dragon's Rage'' will not knock back killed champions that enter a {{tip|zombie state}} upon dying, or a {{ci|Yone}} with his {{ai|E|Yone|Spirit Form}} active.
* ''Dragon's Rage'' will knock back killed champions even if they were immune to the {{tip|airborne|displacement}} at the time of being hit (e.g. with {{tip|displacement immune|displacement immunity}} or {{tip|cc-immune|crowd control immunity}}).
* If ''Dragon's Rage's'' primary target is slain by the ability, their death timer and animation are deferred until their corpse's displacement ends.
{{Unit-targeted cancel conditions}}
}}

